        "original_id": "7b794935-7135-53ba-8c2c-bf83c264464d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: \"A Pair of Brown Eyes\", \"Rum Sodomy & the Lash\", \"Wild Mountain Thyme\", \"Will Ye Go Lassie Go\"\n- People: Shane MacGowan, Francis McPeake, Francis McPeake 1st\n- Organizations: The Pogues\n- Concepts: Scottish folk music, traditional Irish folk style\n\nFacts:\n- Francis McPeake 1st wrote \"Wild Mountain Thyme\" for his wife.\n- \"Wild Mountain Thyme\", also known as \"Will Ye Go Lassie Go\", is a Scottish folk song.\n- \"A Pair of Brown Eyes\" appeared on The Pogues' second album, \"Rum Sodomy & the Lash\".\n- Shane MacGowan, front man of The Pogues, composed \"A Pair of Brown Eyes\" using the melody of \"Wild Mountain Thyme\".\n- The source describes \"Wild Mountain Thyme\" as a song by Francis McPeake in a traditional Irish folk style.",
